<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

<title>VECTOR Systems Dynamics | Engineering Operating Model</title>

<meta
  name="description"
  content="VECTOR Systems Dynamics — an advanced control-theory framework for engineering focus, bottleneck elimination, system leverage, and compound learning."
>

<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

<style>

/* =========================================================
   LIGHT DESIGN SYSTEM (High-Clarity Engineering Slate)
========================================================= */

:root{
    --bg:#f8fafc;
    --bg-alt:#f1f5f9;
    --panel:#ffffff;

    --text:#0f172a;
    --muted:#475569;

    --accent:#2563eb;
    --accent-dark:#1d4ed8;
    --accent-soft:rgba(37,99,235,.07);
    --accent-border:rgba(37,99,235,.22);

    --teal:#0d9488;

    --border:#e2e8f0;
    --border-strong:#cbd5e1;

    --radius:16px;
    --radius-sm:10px;

    --shadow:
        0 10px 30px -5px rgba(15,23,42,.05),
        0 4px 12px -2px rgba(15,23,42,.02);

    --mono:"JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    --sans:"Plus Jakarta Sans", sans-serif;
}


/* =========================================================
   RESET & BASE
========================================================= */

*{
    margin:0;
    padding:0;
    box-sizing:border-box;
}

html{
    scroll-behavior:smooth;
}

body{
    min-height:100vh;
    background:var(--bg);
    color:var(--text);
    font-family:var(--sans);
    line-height:1.65;
    overflow-x:hidden;
}

/* Crisp grid backdrop */
body::before{
    content:"";
    position:fixed;
    inset:0;
    pointer-events:none;
    opacity:.5;
    background-image:
        linear-gradient(rgba(226,232,240,.6) 1px, transparent 1px),
        linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(226,232,240,.6) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size:36px 36px;
    mask-image:linear-gradient(to bottom, black 30%, transparent 90%);
}


/* =========================================================
   GLOBAL UTILITIES
========================================================= */

.container{
    width:min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px));
    margin:auto;
}

.section-block{
    padding:60px 0;
    clear:both;
}

a{
    color:inherit;
    text-decoration:none;
}


/* =========================================================
   HEADER
========================================================= */

header{
    padding:20px 0;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
    background:rgba(255,255,255,.9);
    backdrop-filter:blur(16px);
    position:sticky;
    top:0;
    z-index:100;
}

.nav{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:space-between;
    align-items:center;
}

.brand{
    display:flex;
    align-items:center;
    gap:12px;
}

.brand-mark{
    width:36px;
    height:36px;
    border-radius:8px;
    background:var(--accent);
    color:#ffffff;
    display:grid;
    place-items:center;
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-weight:700;
    box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(37,99,235,.3);
}

.brand-text strong{
    display:block;
    font-size:.9rem;
    letter-spacing:.02em;
    color:var(--text);
}

.brand-text span{
    color:var(--muted);
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:.65rem;
}

.status{
    display:flex;
    align-items:center;
    gap:8px;
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:.72rem;
    color:var(--muted);
    background:var(--bg-alt);
    padding:6px 12px;
    border-radius:100px;
    border:1px solid var(--border);
}

.status-dot{
    width:8px;
    height:8px;
    border-radius:50%;
    background:var(--teal);
}


/* =========================================================
   HERO & VECTOR ENGINE VISUAL
========================================================= */

.hero-grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:1.1fr 0.9fr;
    gap:40px;
    align-items:center;
}

.eyebrow{
    display:inline-flex;
    align-items:center;
    gap:8px;
    background:var(--accent-soft);
    border:1px solid var(--accent-border);
    border-radius:100px;
    padding:6px 14px;
    font-family:var(--mono);
    color:var(--accent);
    font-size:.7rem;
    font-weight:600;
    margin-bottom:20px;
}

.hero h1{
    font-size:clamp(2.4rem, 4.5vw, 4rem);
    line-height:1.1;
    letter-spacing:-.03em;
    font-weight:800;
    color:var(--text);
}

.hero h1 span{
    color:var(--accent);
    display:block;
}

.hero-copy{
    color:var(--muted);
    font-size:1.05rem;
    margin-top:20px;
    line-height:1.6;
}

.hero-tags{
    display:flex;
    gap:8px;
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    margin-top:28px;
}

.tag{
    padding:6px 12px;
    border:1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius:6px;
    color:var(--muted);
    background:var(--panel);
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:.7rem;
}

/* Simplified, Structured Engine Diagram (No position absolute overlap) */

.engine-card{
    background:var(--panel);
    border:1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius:var(--radius);
    padding:28px;
    box-shadow:var(--shadow);
}

.engine-header{
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:.75rem;
    font-weight:700;
    color:var(--accent);
    letter-spacing:.05em;
    margin-bottom:16px;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom:10px;
}

.engine-nodes{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap:12px;
}

.engine-node{
    background:var(--bg-alt);
    border:1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius:var(--radius-sm);
    padding:12px 16px;
}

.engine-node-code{
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-weight:700;
    font-size:.85rem;
    color:var(--accent-dark);
}

.engine-node-desc{
    font-size:.78rem;
    color:var(--muted);
    margin-top:2px;
}


/* =========================================================
   SECTION HEADERS
========================================================= */

.section-head{
    margin-bottom:32px;
}

.section-number{
    color:var(--accent);
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:.72rem;
    font-weight:700;
    letter-spacing:.08em;
}

.section-head h2{
    font-size:clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    line-height:1.2;
    letter-spacing:-.02em;
    margin-top:6px;
}

.section-head p{
    color:var(--muted);
    margin-top:10px;
    max-width:680px;
    font-size:1rem;
}


/* =========================================================
   VECTOR PIPELINE CARDS
========================================================= */

.pipeline{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap:20px;
}

.pipeline-card{
    background:var(--panel);
    border:1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius:var(--radius);
    padding:28px;
    box-shadow:var(--shadow);
    transition:transform .2s ease, border-color .2s ease;
}

.pipeline-card:hover{
    transform:translateY(-3px);
    border-color:var(--accent-border);
}

.vector-tag{
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:.7rem;
    font-weight:700;
    color:var(--accent);
    margin-bottom:12px;
}

.pipeline-card h3{
    font-size:1.15rem;
    margin-bottom:8px;
}

.pipeline-card p{
    color:var(--muted);
    font-size:.88rem;
    line-height:1.6;
}


/* =========================================================
   MATH & CONTROL THEORY MODEL
========================================================= */

.model-grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
    gap:20px;
}

.equation-box{
    background:var(--panel);
    border:1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius:var(--radius);
    padding:32px;
    box-shadow:var(--shadow);
}

.formula{
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:1.3rem;
    color:var(--accent-dark);
    margin:20px 0;
    padding:16px;
    background:var(--bg-alt);
    border-radius:var(--radius-sm);
    text-align:center;
    border:1px solid var(--border);
}

.model-note{
    font-size:.85rem;
    color:var(--muted);
}


/* =========================================================
   SECTOR MATRIX
========================================================= */

.matrix-wrap{
    background:var(--panel);
    border:1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius:var(--radius);
    overflow-x:auto;
    box-shadow:var(--shadow);
}

.matrix{
    width:100%;
    border-collapse:collapse;
    text-align:left;
    min-width:600px;
}

.matrix th, .matrix td{
    padding:18px 24px;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
    border-right:1px solid var(--border);
    font-size:.88rem;
}

.matrix th{
    background:var(--bg-alt);
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:.72rem;
    color:var(--muted);
    text-transform:uppercase;
}

.matrix td:first-child{
    font-weight:700;
    font-family:var(--mono);
    color:var(--accent);
    width:180px;
}


/* =========================================================
   EXECUTION STEPS
========================================================= */

.execution-grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap:20px;
}

.execution-card{
    background:var(--panel);
    border:1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius:var(--radius);
    padding:28px;
    box-shadow:var(--shadow);
}

.step-num{
    width:28px;
    height:28px;
    border-radius:50%;
    background:var(--accent-soft);
    color:var(--accent);
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:.75rem;
    font-weight:700;
    display:grid;
    place-items:center;
    margin-bottom:14px;
}


/* =========================================================
   FOOTER
========================================================= */

footer{
    margin-top:60px;
    padding:40px 0;
    border-top:1px solid var(--border);
    background:var(--panel);
}

.footer-inner{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:space-between;
    align-items:center;
    font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:.72rem;
    color:var(--muted);
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    gap:12px;
}

@media(max-width:850px){
    .hero-grid, .model-grid{
        grid-template-columns:1fr;
    }
}

</style>
</head>


<body>

<!-- HEADER -->
<header>
<div class="container nav">
    <a href="#" class="brand">
        <div class="brand-mark">V</div>
        <div class="brand-text">
            <strong>VECTOR DYNAMICS</strong>
            <span>SYSTEMS ENGINEERING PLAYBOOK</span>
        </div>
    </a>
    <div class="status">
        <span class="status-dot"></span>
        MODEL v2.4 / ACTIVE
    </div>
</div>
</header>


<main class="container">

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="section-block hero">
    <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">
                <span>01</span> CONTROL THEORY &amp; COGNITIVE DYNAMICS
            </div>

            <h1>
                Engineer your
                <span>system output.</span>
            </h1>

            <p class="hero-copy">
                The <strong>VECTOR Framework</strong> redefines individual capability using classical control theory. Output is not a function of effort or motivation—it is a result of structural throughput, friction reduction, and feedback loops.
            </p>

            <div class="hero-tags">
                <span class="tag">V / VELOCITY</span>
                <span class="tag">E / ENERGY</span>
                <span class="tag">C / CONSTRAINTS</span>
                <span class="tag">T / TOOLING</span>
                <span class="tag">O / OUTPUT</span>
                <span class="tag">R / REFINEMENT</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- RESTRUCTURED DIAGRAM (No Overlapping Elements) -->
        <div class="engine-card">
            <div class="engine-header">
                System Dynamics Architecture
            </div>
            <div class="engine-nodes">
                <div class="engine-node">
                    <div class="engine-node-code">V / Velocity</div>
                    <div class="engine-node-desc">Directional rate (dS/dt)</div>
                </div>
                <div class="engine-node">
                    <div class="engine-node-code">E / Energy</div>
                    <div class="engine-node-desc">Cognitive power budget</div>
                </div>
                <div class="engine-node">
                    <div class="engine-node-code">C / Constraints</div>
                    <div class="engine-node-desc">System bottlenecks</div>
                </div>
                <div class="engine-node">
                    <div class="engine-node-code">T / Tooling</div>
                    <div class="engine-node-desc">Leverage multipliers</div>
                </div>
                <div class="engine-node">
                    <div class="engine-node-code">O / Output</div>
                    <div class="engine-node-desc">Verifiable artifacts</div>
                </div>
                <div class="engine-node">
                    <div class="engine-node-code">R / Refinement</div>
                    <div class="engine-node-desc">Closed feedback loop</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


<!-- CORE MODEL -->
<section class="section-block">
    <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-number">02 / CORE PIPELINE</div>
        <h2>Six Structural Variables</h2>
        <p>
            When engineering systems, optimizing a non-bottleneck yields zero net efficiency gains. VECTOR structures execution to eliminate friction at the true constraint.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pipeline">
        <article class="pipeline-card">
            <div class="vector-tag">V / VELOCITY</div>
            <h3>Directional Vector</h3>
            <p>
                Speed without direction is noise. Velocity measures rate of scalar displacement toward high-leverage technical goals, excluding context-switching overhead.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="pipeline-card">
            <div class="vector-tag">E / ENERGY</div>
            <h3>Cognitive Capacity</h3>
            <p>
                Models deep work as a finite power budget. High-cognitive tasks must align with peak mental bandwidth to minimize error rates and technical debt.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="pipeline-card">
            <div class="vector-tag">C / CONSTRAINTS</div>
            <h3>Bottleneck Identification</h3>
            <p>
                Based on Goldratt's Theory of Constraints: total system output is strictly limited by a single bottleneck (e.g., lack of domain clarity or slow build loops).
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="pipeline-card">
            <div class="vector-tag">T / TOOLING</div>
            <h3>Leverage Multipliers</h3>
            <p>
                Infrastructure, scripts, generative tools, and workspace configuration that reduce activation energy and automate deterministic steps.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="pipeline-card">
            <div class="vector-tag">O / OUTPUT</div>
            <h3>Verifiable Artifacts</h3>
            <p>
                The measurable yield of the system: production code, published papers, built hardware, or tested modules. Unverified work equals zero yield.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="pipeline-card">
            <div class="vector-tag">R / REFINEMENT</div>
            <h3>Closed-Loop Feedback</h3>
            <p>
                Using retro metrics and transfer functions to adjust future work sessions. Converts operational errors into system-level preventative rules.
            </p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>


<!-- MATHEMATICAL MODEL -->
<section class="section-block">
    <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-number">03 / MATHEMATICAL FORMULATION</div>
        <h2>System Dynamics &amp; Feedback Transfer</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="model-grid">
        <div class="equation-box">
            <div class="section-number">SYSTEM OUTPUT TRANSFER FUNCTION</div>
            <div class="formula">
                Y(s) = [ (E · T) / C ] × H(s)
            </div>
            <p class="model-note">
                Where <strong>Y(s)</strong> is net yield, <strong>E</strong> is available energy, <strong>T</strong> is tooling leverage, <strong>C</strong> is constraint impedance, and <strong>H(s)</strong> is the transfer function representing closed-loop learning efficiency.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="equation-box">
            <div class="section-number">KEY TAKEAWAY FOR ENGINEERS</div>
            <p style="margin-top:15px; color:var(--muted);">
                If your constraint <strong>C</strong> approaches infinity (e.g., blocked dependencies, unclear requirements), your total system output <strong>Y(s)</strong> drops toward zero, regardless of how much energy <strong>E</strong> or tooling <strong>T</strong> you apply.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


<!-- TRANSLATION MATRIX -->
<section class="section-block">
    <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-number">04 / APPLICATION MATRIX</div>
        <h2>Domain Translation</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="matrix-wrap">
        <table class="matrix">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Variable</th>
                    <th>Software / Architecture</th>
                    <th>Systems Engineering</th>
                    <th>Research / R&amp;D</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Constraint (C)</td>
                    <td>Slow CI/CD, vague requirements</td>
                    <td>Material lead times, tolerances</td>
                    <td>Noisy data, unverified hypotheses</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Tooling (T)</td>
                    <td>AST generators, custom CLI scripts</td>
                    <td>CAD templates, automation rigs</td>
                    <td>Statistical models, pipeline scripts</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Output (O)</td>
                    <td>Tested production PRs</td>
                    <td>Validated physical prototypes</td>
                    <td>Peer-reviewed technical briefs</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>


<!-- EXECUTION PROTOCOL -->
<section class="section-block">
    <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-number">05 / OPERATIONAL EXECUTION</div>
        <h2>Daily System Protocol</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="execution-grid">
        <div class="execution-card">
            <div class="step-num">1</div>
            <h3>Isolate the Primary Constraint</h3>
            <p style="color:var(--muted); font-size:.88rem; margin-top:6px;">
                Before opening an editor or tool, define the single bottleneck preventing completion. Do not optimize secondary tasks.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="execution-card">
            <div class="step-num">2</div>
            <h3>Minimize Friction via Tooling</h3>
            <p style="color:var(--muted); font-size:.88rem; margin-top:6px;">
                Pre-configure workspace scripts, environments, and templates so deep work can begin with minimal activation energy.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

</main>


<!-- FOOTER -->
<footer>
    <div class="container footer-inner">
        <div>VECTOR SYSTEMS DYNAMICS PLAYBOOK</div>
        <div>OPTIMIZED FOR CLARITY &amp; PERFORMANCE</div>
    </div>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
